# Peka — Level Design: Act 2 (Test — "The Climb Begins")

> Companion to `game-design.md` / `story.md`. Follows `level-act1.md`.
> The pair leaves the nadir and starts **climbing**. Act 2 *tests* the Act-1
> verbs in harder combinations, separates the players more, and adds environmental
> elements that compose with gravity. No new core mechanics (kit stays run/jump/flip).
> Every room **impossible solo**; every hazard **deterministic & telegraphed**
> (death = full restart, GDD §3).

**Legend** (see `level-act1.md` for base symbols)
```
═══ surface   · · · lethal gap   ▒ shadow (lethal)   P player
▭ plate-held platform   ◇ switch   ⊟ crusher (fixed rhythm)
║ pulley/linked platform   ✦ light (far above)
```

---

## 2.1 "Counterweight Ascent" — linked geometry (NEW)

A vertical shaft. A pulley links two platforms: weight on the floor platform
**raises** the ceiling platform, and vice-versa. The halves ride opposite ends,
lifting *each other* up the shaft in stages.

```
═══╗   [▭ceiling]~~pulley~~        ║ as P1 weighs down the floor pad,
   ║        ↑                      ║ the ceiling pad rises with P2 on it
   ║        ║linked                ║ — then they swap to climb the next stage
   ║        ↓                      ║
═══╝   [▭floor, P1]                ║
```
- **Solve:** P1 rides the floor platform down → lifts P2 (ceiling) up; P2 dismounts higher, takes a floor-pad above, lifts P1; leapfrog upward.
- **Impossible solo:** the pulley needs weight on *both* ends, alternately.
- **Tests:** coordinated weight + flip + trust; introduces linked geometry cleanly.

